use std
into look_bench.amni

Imports: os, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes and gfx.scene3d.

`fn num(s const byte[:]) real` parses a real with `parse_flt` (0 when it does not parse).

`fn has(list const byte[:], word const byte[:]) bool` is true when `word` is one of the comma-separated words of `list`.

`fn gpu_ns(path const byte[:], ns real[>..]&)` clears `ns`, reads the file at `path` (nothing when it cannot be read) and, for every line that starts with "submit", pushes the integer in its last space-separated field as a real.

`fn median(xs real[>..]) real` and `fn p95(xs real[>..]) real` sort a copy of `xs` ascending and return its element at index len / 2, and at index min(len - 1, len * 95 / 100); 0 for an empty list.

`fn studio()` sets the Amni-Companion studio light: `s3d::sun = s3d::Sun { to_sun: linalg::unit3(float3 { 2.3, 3.0, 1.3 }), rgb: float3 { 3.1, 3.1, 3.1 }, shadows: true, shadow_far: 10.0, map_size: 2048 }`; `s3d::lights.clear()`; `s3d::add_light(float3 { -11.9, 14.3, -16.7 }, float3 { 371.0, 241.0, 936.0 }, 1000.0)` (rim), `s3d::add_light(float3 { -17.3, 8.65, 15.85 }, float3 { 124.0, 136.0, 169.0 }, 1000.0)` (fill), `s3d::add_light(float3 { 0.0, 9.0, 23.0 }, float3 { 600.0, 600.0, 600.0 }, 1000.0)` (room); `s3d::sky = s3d::Sky { zenith: float3 { 0.0308, 0.0366, 0.0967 }, horizon: float3 { 0.0154, 0.0182, 0.0436 }, ground: float3 { 0.0082, 0.0096, 0.0185 }, ambient: 2.5, draw: true }`; `s3d::look.exposure = 1.12`, `s3d::look.bloom = 0.0`, `s3d::look.desaturate = 0.0`, `s3d::look.curve = 1`.

`fn features(f const byte[:])` applies the comma-separated feature words in `f` with `has`: "pcss" sets `s3d::sun.angle = 0.07` and `s3d::sun.reach = 1.0`; "wide" sets `s3d::sun.angle = 0.17`; "fit" sets `s3d::sun.fit = true`; "taa" sets `s3d::temporal = 1`; "noao" sets `s3d::look.ssao = false`; "gtao" sets `s3d::ao_mode = 1`; "contact" sets `s3d::sun.contact = 0.07`; "local" turns the first two lights (rim and fill) into shadowed spots aimed at (0, 0.9, 0): for k in 0 and 1 set `s3d::lights[k].kind = 1`, `s3d::lights[k].dir = linalg::unit3(float3 { 0.0, 0.9, 0.0 } - s3d::lights[k].pos)`, `s3d::lights[k].cone = 0.08` and `s3d::lights[k].shadows = true`; "point" sets `s3d::lights[0].shadows = true` and `s3d::lights[1].shadows = true` with the lights left as points; "direct" sets `s3d::debug_view = 5`; "noshadow" sets `s3d::sun.shadows = false`; "hires" sets `s3d::sun.map_size = 8192`; "sunonly" sets `s3d::lights.clear()` and `s3d::sky.ambient = 0.0`; "soft" calls `s3d::studio_soft(float3 { 0.8, 0.81, 0.84 }, 2.0)` (the soft gray studio preset); "expo" sets `s3d::look.auto_exposure = true`; "bright" multiplies `s3d::sun.rgb` by 4 and every light's `rgb` by 4; "dof" sets `s3d::dof_aperture = 0.004` and `s3d::dof_focus` to the distance from `s3d::view.eye` to `s3d::view.target`; "mblur" sets `s3d::motion_blur = 0.5`; "lut" calls `warm_lut()` and sets `s3d::look.lut = 1.0`; "idlut" sets `s3d::look.lut = 1.0` (the identity table scene3d makes at init); "noso" sets `s3d::spec_occlusion = false`; "ssr" sets `s3d::ssr_on = true`; "dbgso" sets `s3d::debug_view = 9`; "dbgssr" sets `s3d::debug_view = 10`; "ambient" sets `s3d::debug_view = 4`.

`fn warm_lut()` builds a 17 x 17 x 17 RGBA8 grading table (red fastest, then green, then blue; v = index / 16.0 per channel) mapping (r, g, b) to (min(1, r * 1.06 + 0.02), g, b * 0.88 + 0.03), each times 255 rounded, alpha 255, and passes it to `s3d::set_lut(px[..], 17)`.

`fn orbit(k int)` moves `s3d::view.eye` around `s3d::view.target` about the vertical axis by 0.03 radians times k from the eye it had before the first call (keep that first eye in a module variable `eye0` with a flag `have_eye0`).

`main()`: arguments (after the program name) are the .glb path, the output .png path ("-" for none), width, height, eye x y z, target x y z, fov_y (radians), the feature words, the number of timed frames and, optionally, a floor flag (a[14] == "floor"). Let `w` and `h` be the width and height as int. Set `gltf::lazy_pixels = true`. Open a headless device of w x h with `gfx::open_headless` (on failure print "look_bench: no device: " plus `gfx::error()` and return). Load the glb with `gltf::load` (negative: print "look_bench: load failed" and return). `let it = s3d::add(asset)` and `s3d::place(it, gfx::mat4_identity)`. When the floor flag is set: `var fm = shapes::material(float3 { 0.55, 0.55, 0.56 }, 0.0, 0.9)`, `fm.no_shadow = true`, `let fl = s3d::add(shapes::plane(3.0, fm))`, `s3d::place(fl, gfx::mat4_identity)`. Set `s3d::view` to an `s3d::Camera` from the eye to the target with up (0, 1, 0), that fov_y, near 0.05 and far 100. Call `studio()` then `features(a[12])`. `s3d::init(w, h)`; make `let out = gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`. Let `spin = has(a[12], "mblur")`. Keep a frame counter `fk` starting at 0; before every `s3d::render(out)` call in this program, when spin, call `orbit(fk)` and add 1 to fk. Render `if s3d::temporal != 0 { 48 } else { 3 }` frames with `s3d::render(out)` and `gfx::flush()`. When the feature words include "expo", print "look_bench: exposure ", `s3d::exposure_now()`. When the feature words include "info", print "look_bench: cascades live ", `s3d::cascade_live`, " ends ", `s3d::cascade_end[0]`, " ", `s3d::cascade_end[1]`, " ", `s3d::cascade_end[2]`. When the output path is not "-", save it with `gfx::save_png(out, path)` and print "saved " plus the path. Let `n = num(a[13]) as int`. When n > 0: render 30 warmup frames (each `s3d::render(out)` then `gfx::flush()`); read the environment variable HELIUM_GPUTIME with `env` into `log` (have_log when it is set and not empty); when have_log, `gpu_ns(log[..], before)` and let `first = before.len`; then time n frames, each `let t = gfx::time()`, `s3d::render(out)`, `gfx::flush()`, pushing `(gfx::time() - t) * 1000.0` onto `wall`. Print "look_bench: " plus the features, " wall ms median ", median(wall), " p95 ", p95(wall). When have_log: `gpu_ns(log[..], all)`; let `k = all.len - first`; when k is 0 or k % n != 0 print "look_bench: gpu submits cannot be split" else, with `per = k / n`, for each frame f sum `all[first + f * per + j]` over j below per divided by 1e6 into `each`, and print "look_bench: " plus the features, " gpu ms median ", median(each), " p95 ", p95(each), " (", per, " submits/frame)".
